\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 Old-Time Newspaper Rivalry With Two New Stars Will Face First Battle in Court\b0\par\par\uc2 By Katie Robertson \par \uc2 920 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 May 2026\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 6\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 First, \uc2 The Star\uc2  was born. Now, The Washington Star is reborn. Both are hoping to win readers ceded by recent layoffs at \uc2 The Washington Post\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 An old-fashioned newspaper war is brewing in the nation's capital.\par \par \uc2 The Washington Star, a newspaper that stopped printing more than 40 years ago, has started publishing again under the ownership of Dovid Efune, a media executive and publisher of The New York Sun.\par \par \uc2 It comes just weeks after the politics site NOTUS announced it would rebrand as The Star and expand its mission to cover local news and sports in Washington.\par \par \uc2 The two closely named rivals plan to take on a much more established competitor: The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 , which is owned by the \uc2 Amazon\uc2  founder \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2  and recently cut its staff by a third.\par \par \uc2 ''We're reviving one of the great and epic rivalries of American journalism,'' Mr. Efune said in an interview. ''For decades, \uc2 The Star\uc2  was The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 's fiercest competitor and an important editorial and ideological counterweight in the press in our nation's capital.''\par \par \uc2 The outlets, and their promise of new jobs, are arriving at a tough time for the media industry, when many publications are laying off staff and trying to adjust their businesses for plummeting search traffic and a race to notch up paid subscribers. The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  laid off more than 300 of its 800 journalists in February after losing more than $100 million a year, retreating from much of its metro and sports coverage.\par \par \uc2 The rivalry has already reached the courts. On Thursday, Mr. Efune filed a trademark infringement lawsuit against NOTUS for its planned use of the Star moniker.\par \par \uc2 The Washington Star was a conservative-leaning afternoon newspaper that published for 128 years until it went into bankruptcy and shut down in 1981. The Post snapped up The Washington Star's former headquarters and printing presses in the bankruptcy sale.\par \par \uc2 The new Washington Star has started publishing on \uc2 Substack\uc2 , and Mr. Efune said that he intended to have a custom website live within the next two months and offer a weekend print newspaper by the end of the year. Mr. Efune said that he was interviewing candidates for multiple roles and planned to hire up to 50 full-time journalists and contributors.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Efune, a former top editor of the Jewish newspaper The Algemeiner, has some experience with reinvigorating old papers. For the past few years, he has focused on The New York Sun, a defunct broadsheet that shut down in 2008. The outlet now publishes online and has a weekly print edition, and it counts two million subscribers, ''tens of thousands of which are paid,'' according to a Thursday memo from Mr. Efune that said the paper was profitable.\par \par \uc2 The Washington Star will publish under the oversight of The Sun's newsroom until an editor in chief is named. It will be ideologically aligned but distinct, according to a Thursday memo from Mr. Efune to the paper's staff.\par \par \uc2 In an editorial, Mr. Efune wrote that The Washington Star's remake had been ''some years in the making'' and that his priority was to ''stay true to the editorial legacy of The Star,'' which he described as supporting ''limited government'' and opposing ''bureaucratic corruption and federal overreach.''\par \par \uc2 The Washington Star will face an equally determined competitor in \uc2 Robert Allbritton\uc2 , who is underwriting The Star. Mr. Allbritton is the billionaire co-founder of Politico. His father, Joe Allbritton, owned The Washington Star from 1975 to 1978.\par \par \uc2 The junior Mr. Allbritton founded the nonprofit Allbritton Journalism Institute in 2023, intending to train up young journalists. The institute publishes NOTUS, which currently covers political news.\par \par \uc2 Tim Grieve\uc2 , the editor in chief of NOTUS, told \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  last month that NOTUS would relaunch as The Star in the first week of June and had plans to more than double its newsroom to 95 journalists by the end of the year. NOTUS has recently hired a number of prominent Post reporters and plans to aggressively expand its coverage in Washington.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Efune, who was recently a bidder for The Daily Telegraph in Britain, said the launch of Mr. Allbritton's The Star did not deter him and instead ''accelerated our timeline to scale up.''\par \par \uc2 But he is also suing over its name.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit states that Mr. Allbritton's familial connection to the old Washington Star as well as the fact that the two outlets will operate in the same marketplace with a similar name will cause confusion and could deceive consumers. The complaint was filed in U.S. District Court for the Eastern District of Virginia.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Efune, who has owned the trademark for The Washington Star since 2024, discussed selling it to NOTUS in March and April, though the talks did not end in a deal, according to the complaint. NOTUS then said it would rebrand as The Star later in April.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Efune declined to comment on the lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 A NOTUS spokesman said in a statement on Thursday that NOTUS intended to vigorously defend against the claims.\par \par \uc2 ''The entity does not and cannot own the word 'Star,' which has been used by and associated with dozens of media publications for over 100 years,'' the spokesman said. ''The entity itself only even claims to have recently adopted 'The Washington Star,' decades after numerous other 'Star' publications have been using 'Star' marks.''\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020260529em5t0003x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
