\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 The Digest\b0\par\par\uc2 By Reuters \par \uc2 468 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 May 2026\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 REGULATION\par \par \uc2 Volvo and California Settle Emissions Inquiry\par \par \uc2 Volvo Group\uc2  agreed on Monday to a $197 million settlement with the \uc2 California Air Resources Board\uc2  over alleged violations of the state's heavy duty engine regulations.\par \par \uc2 The settlement resolves allegations that Volvo failed to properly disclose auxiliary emission control devices in over 10,000 of its 2010-2016 model year heavy-duty engines in California that resulted in emissions in excess of regulatory limits, the board said.\par \par \uc2 Volvo will pay $13 million in civil penalties, $71 million to CARB's Air Pollution Control Fund, spend $108 million on California emissions-reduction projects and reimburse $5 million of CARB's costs, the truck maker said.\par \par \uc2 As part of the settlement, Volvo will make software updates and a partial warranty extension available for about 7,200 engines in California. Volvo said the settlement is without admission of liability and that an internal review found no evidence of bad faith. REUTERS\par \par \uc2 RETAIL\par \par \uc2 Lululemon\uc2  Says Talks With Founder Collapsed\par \par \uc2 Lululemon Athletica\uc2  tried but failed to settle its bitter proxy fight with its founder as recently as last week when the apparel retailer said its founder made escalating demands, according to a Monday regulatory filing.\par \par \uc2 The company said it delayed filing its definitive proxy statement in hopes of reaching an agreement with \uc2 Chip Wilson\uc2 , who founded the maker of stretchy yoga pants in 1998 and has recently criticized management for having lost the company's ''cool'' factor.\par \par \uc2 Shares are down 62 percent in the last 12 months as design missteps and fading brand appeal eroded its edge, and it recently hired a new C.E.O.\par \par \uc2 In its first detailed public rebuttal since the battle began late last year, \uc2 Lululemon\uc2  said Mr. Wilson, who left the board in 2015, has ''outdated perspectives'' about how to position \uc2 Lululemon\uc2  as well as ''troubling conflicts of interest.'' REUTERS\par \par \uc2 RETAIL\par \par \uc2 IKEA Franchiser to Cut 850 Jobs as Sales Fall\par \par \uc2 Inter IKEA\uc2 , which franchises the Swedish budget home furniture brand in 63 countries, is laying off 850 workers in a cost-cutting drive as consumer demand falls and the blue big-box retailer works to become more efficient and bring down prices.\par \par \uc2 The vast company manages the sourcing of \uc2 IKEA\uc2  products from factories around the world and supplies 13 franchisees operating \uc2 IKEA\uc2  stores. It has been squeezed by rising costs and U.S. tariffs, and is in the midst of a strategic shift from big suburban warehouse stores to more smaller city-center locations as it tries to draw back shoppers.\par \par \uc2 ''We need to become faster, shorten the decision-making processes, and simply concentrate our efforts on these priorities,'' said Henrik Elm, \uc2 Inter IKEA\uc2 's chief financial officer.\par \par \uc2 The cuts represent around 3 percent of \uc2 Inter IKEA\uc2 's 27,500 employees. REUTERS\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020260519em5j0007k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
